Z||000002||ChopTop||11-13-2001||02:40 PM||||If GM has to have a tiny two-seater, bring back the Fiero.<BR>---------------------------------------------<BR>Here, here!!!!! Being a Fiero fan, I'd LOVE to see what it could be with Mr. Lutz at the wheel!!!<P>I'd say most of the posters sound knowledgeable about sports cars, and I'd bet most of them are aware of the Fiero's history.  Generally, when the Fiero is mentioned it almost always done in a negative way, with more negative comments to follow.  This hasn't happend (yet) in the thread, which is refreshing for a change.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||11-14-2001||03:03 PM||||At least they mentioned it.  As much as I like my Fiero, they do own Corvettes and if I had the chance to trade a Fiero for a C5 I think I would.  So I wouldn't be very offended if they thought more of their Vettes than my Fiero.  Fortunately, most Vette owners I know or have run into always are complimentary towards my Fiero.<P>As for their discussion on the Vette... I don't think Mr. Lutz would turn it into an S2000.  I think what he is talking about is getting rid of some extra bulk.  The rear end of the car is rather big (wide!).  If what they do makes the car lighter, faster, handle better, and all around more fun to drive then there shouldn't be too many complaints.  They ned to trust Lutz a little.  He did get the Viper right, and I am sure he isn't about to mess up the Vette!  He knows what he is doing. <P>Now about brining back the Fiero...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-14-2001||03:15 PM||||your rite formula. A Corvette is waaaaaaaayyy to heavy for what it is. It would really be a sports car if they could lose about 1,000 pnds. They prob could lose most of it in the body. Try lifting a corvette nose, that things gotta weight 4-5 hundred pounds by itself. Id say go with a lot of aluminum and carbon fiber in body construction.||||reg||1
